{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Beatles 1967 1970 feels like a natural next choice after Sgt. Pepper's because it expands on music by an artist I have already chosen.",
    "Cat Stevens feels especially relevant alongside Simon & Garfunkel and Jonathan Edwards because the acoustic songwriting connects those choices. Neil Diamond and Chronicle also fit my repeated interest in familiar older songs and greatest-hits collections."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Johnny Cash Live at San Quentin feels less relevant because a live country performance does not match the melodic pop, folk, and classic rock collections I want right now.",
    "Partners and 20th Century Masters give me too little information about the music to feel a clear connection. Duets and Christmas Together have plausible links to my history, but I would need to know the performers and songs before choosing them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Being an older recording or a hits collection seems to count too heavily; the artist and musical style matter more than those broad similarities.",
    "My choices of Cheek to Cheek and A Very Special Christmas seem to have been extended into interest in other duet and Christmas albums without enough evidence that their performers or songs appeal to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie makes acoustic songwriting a stronger reason for me to choose something than its age alone.",
    "My recent Christmas choice makes seasonal music relevant, but my repeated choices of folk, rock, and older pop collections still guide which albums I would choose first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in familiar older music, but some stretch that interest beyond the artists, songwriting, and styles that make me want to listen."
}"}
